// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential NTDS.DIT Dump Via Dsdbutil.EXE
// Sigma ID: 4aefbb19-11bd-4909-ae64-70ca9943369b
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: EinLamYe
// Date: 2026-06-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1003.003
// Description: Detects usage of dsdbutil.exe to create a snapshot or IFM media set of the Active Directory
//   database (NTDS.dit). Threat actors abuse this signed LOLBin on Domain Controllers to obtain
//   domain credential material for offline extraction.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate Active Directory maintenance or backup snapshots performed by administrators
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/Dsdbutil/
//   - https://pentestlab.blog/tag/dsdbutil/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/8e7b36a9de00c979a098f16eb29c1c22fb63cb4b/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_dsdbutil_ntds_dump.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\dsdbutil.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "dsdbutil.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "snapshot" or ProcessCommandLine contains "create full" or ProcessCommandLine contains " ifm")
